<title>FINLAND: Clinton, Yeltsin start summit talks.</title>
<headline>Clinton, Yeltsin start summit talks.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. President Bill Clinton and Russian President Boris Yeltsin started summit talks on Friday that were expected to focus on the bitterly divisive issue of NATO enlargement.</p>
<p>The two leaders met at a secluded villa, surrounded by pines and overlooking the partly-frozen Baltic Sea. The house is the official residence of President Martti Ahtisaari, who greeted both men before leaving them to their talks.</p>
</text>
